2.25.1

Code statements:
```dts
&gpio0 {
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
	ti,no-idle-on-init;
```

Code statements:
&gpio0 {
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
	ti,no-idle-on-init;

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0 {
	ti,no-idle-on-init;
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
The flags `ti,no-idle-on-init` and `ti,no-reset-on-init` were incorrectly placed within the `&gpio0` node instead of being defined at the interconnect target module level. This misplacement caused warnings during the device tree compilation, indicating that these flags should be at the module level, which could lead to improper initialization of the GPIO0 configuration.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0_target {
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
By moving the `ti,no-reset-on-init` flag to the `&gpio0_target` node, the flags are now correctly defined at the interconnect target module level. This change resolves the warnings and ensures that the GPIO0 configuration is properly initialized without misconfiguration.

